The '''1996 Football League Cup final''' took place on 24 March 1996 at [[Wembley Stadium (1923)|Wembley Stadium]] and was contested between [[Aston Villa F.C.|Aston Villa]] and [[Leeds United A.F.C.|Leeds United]]. This was the 36th final and the 30th to be played at Wembley. Aston Villa had won the trophy two years earlier, while Leeds' last victory was in their only final appearance in [[1968 Football League Cup final|1968]].

In the first half the teams were separated by a goal from [[Savo Milošević]]. After half-time, Leeds United tired and Aston Villa took advantage to eventually win 3–0. Goals from [[Ian Taylor (footballer, born 1968)|Ian Taylor]] and [[Dwight Yorke]] completed the scoring.<ref name=Indy-report>{{cite news|title=Milosevic gives Villa a touch of magic|url=https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/milosevic-gives-villa-a-touch-of-magic-1343925.html|publisher=The Independent|date=25 March 1996|access-date=8 May 2012}}</ref> This was the beginning of the end for Leeds United manager [[Howard Wilkinson]], as he was heckled by the club's fans for his and the team's failure. However, it was Villa's fifth success in the competition, at the time equalling the record set by [[Liverpool F.C.|Liverpool]]. This was the last time that Aston Villa won a major trophy until [[2026 UEFA Europa League final|30 years later]] when they won the UEFA Europa League in 2026.

